  "texts": {
    "preamble": "V K Pallapothu vs The State Of Ap on 13 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5133 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/accused seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.185 of 2019 of Martur Police Station, Prakasam District, which was registered against him for the offences under Sections 188, 273 of IPC and Secs.59 & 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 09.08.2019 at about 18:00 hours, the S.I of Police along with staff was performing patrolling duties in Martur Village, on credible information about sale of banned tobacco products in Tiffin centre, near Government Hospital, Martur Village and Mandal, they raided and found banned tobacco products in the possession of petitioner, seized the same under a police proceedings, later he arrested him and registered a case in Crime No.185 of 2019 for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
